<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n6629" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀναΐσσω</span></b>  [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ᾰνᾱ</span>], 
			Att.
		
		
			contr.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνᾴσσω</span></b> , used also by <i><span class="en">
			Pi.
		</span></i>:—<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>start up,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μὴ πρὶν ἀναΐξειαν Ἀρήϊοι υἷες
					Ἀχαιῶν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					4.114
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὅτε δὴ . . ἀναΐξειεν
			Ὀδυσσεύς</span> whenever <i>he rose to speak,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				3.216
			</span></i>; of a spring, <i>gush forth,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				22.148
			</span></i>: so in later Poets, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μυελὸς στέρνων
				ἐντὸς ἀνᾴσσων</span>
			<i>springing fresh</i> within the breast, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Ag.</u>
				77
			</span></i> cj. <i><span class="en">
				Herm.
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>Pers.</u>
				96
			</span></i> cj. Brunck; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀρθοὶ ἀνῇξαν πάντες</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Hel.</u>
					1600
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βωμὸς ἀνᾴσσων</span> an altar
				<i>rising up,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>O.</u>
				13.107
			</span></i>.—Rare in Prose, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀναΐσσει νόσημα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hp.
					<u>Prog.</u>
					19
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνᾴξας,</span> of a hare, <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Cyn.</u>
				6.17
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> c. acc.,
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀναΐξας . . ἅρμα καὶ ἵππους</span>
			<i>having leapt upon</i> it, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				24.440
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			
				Act.
			, <i>cause to start up,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνήϊξεν δὲ φέβεσθαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Opp.
					<u>C.</u>
					1.107
				</span></i>
			.</div>
